sair-eqt2-stage2-solver
  Haobo Ma, Wenlin Zhang and Manuel Israel Cázares
  https://github.com/the-omega-institute/sair-eqt2-stage2-solver, commit 4bf87e3

  hard2_0027_zero.lean
    Derived from the certificate with SHA-256 prefix dd26586983db in that
    repository's results/,
    as emitted by austin_counterexample in submission/solver.py.
    Kept byte for byte: def f, the statement of f_1659, impl, f_2473 and the
    final def submission.
    Changed: the lemma block, with its helper lemmas replaced and its proofs
    redone from the fuel definitions of Nat.mod and Nat.modCore, so that the
    certificate closes over no axioms.
    The file carries no notice of its own, because a comment would change the
    bytes the judge accepted.

  austin_f_lemmas_hand.txt
    A replacement for the string _AUSTIN_F_LEMMAS in submission/solver.py.
    It keeps def f and the statements of f_1659, mod_two_ne_down_to and
    mod_two_eq_down_to, drops the other six mod_two lemmas, adds 14 new ones, and
    redoes every proof as above. No notice in the file, because its text is pasted
    into certificates.

  ledger_extract.py, true_extract.py, cert_run.py, results/
    Read that repository's results/ tree. Only aggregates and per-problem status
    are recorded here. No certificate from the ledger is included, apart from the
    two files above. ledger_extract.py's TEMPLATE holds the fixed frame of the
    finOpTable certificates, with no table.

  The packed form itself is the shape make_false_code_arith in
  submission/solver.py already writes.


Equational Theories Project
  https://github.com/teorth/equational_theories

  hard2_0027_zero.lean
    def f is that project's op_1659_4315, in
    equational_theories/ManuallyProved/Equation1659.lean, lines 21 to 28, as the
    certificate above uses it.

  The packed reader
    (t / n^i) % n was written by Joachim Breitner for that project in September
    2024, as opOfTable behind memoFinOp in MemoFinOp.lean (first in commit
    937546f, on the branch of PR #19; on main through PR #110), for kernel
    reduction speed. No code is copied from it here.

  NoFinite.lean
    The finite statement is already in that project as
    Eq1133.Finite.Equation1167_implies_Equation1096 plus three general
    implications. The proof here is a different route.

  infinite-map/
    infinite-map.tsv and facts.tsv cite that project's files and theorems.
    Certificates for pairs it refutes with an explicit construction follow that
    construction's operation, rewritten in core Lean. The 12 translation-invariant
    models on Z are not taken from it.

  The infinite-only list rests on that project's graph.json and finite_graph.json,
  as the header of data/etp/infinite-only.tsv in parsimagma says, and its
  attribution on graph.json's full_entries and the Lean sources at commit e5a88a1.
  The graphs are not vendored; data/etp/PROVENANCE.txt lists what is.


equational-theories-lean-stage2 (the competition's judge)
  https://github.com/SAIRcompetition/equational-theories-lean-stage2, commit 817a465

  judge_run.py, cert_run.py
    Call its verify_answer. No judge code is included.

  memofinop-three-lines.diff, PatchedParserEqual.lean
    A patch to judge/JudgeFinOp/MemoFinOp.lean, and a proof about it that imports that
